# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows writes CRLF into the working
# tree while CI checks out LF. Tests that read repo files and match a pattern
# spanning a line break then pass on CI and fail on a Windows machine — which is
# exactly what `odds-population-schedule.test.ts` did: a red suite that no
# reviewer could reproduce and no CI run would ever catch.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF (autocrlf normalizes on the way in), so
# this changes checkout only, not history.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Left byte-for-byte: these are not text and must never be line-ending munged.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
